# Project structure

`docs/structure.md` is the map of this repo. Read it before searching for where code or static assets live.

When a change adds, removes, renames, or moves a folder, route, feature module, or top-level file that belongs on that map, update `docs/structure.md` in the same change. Update the tree and the "where new code goes" section together.

Skip generated and secret files: `node_modules/`, `.next/`, `next-env.d.ts`, `*.tsbuildinfo`, `.env.local`, `.env.production`.

```text
# Adding /learn/vocabularies
# 1. app/(default)/learn/vocabularies/page.tsx — screen stays beside the page
# 2. app/components/registry.ts if the home page, header, or footer links to it
# 3. docs/structure.md — add the route
```
